# KaleidOS Core options.
#
# Core-level build switches that change the Core's own behaviour or the boot
# image.  Component selection does NOT belong here -- see os/components/Kconfig.

menu "Core options"

config PREEMPT
	bool "Preemptive scheduling"
	default n
	help
	  Let the scheduler preempt a running task on a timer interrupt instead
	  of switching only cooperatively at explicit yield points.  Off by
	  default: cooperative round-robin is the current baseline.

endmenu

menu "Debugging / Testing"

config TRACE
	bool "Structured Core trace"
	default y
	help
	  Compile the structured Core trace (the TraceEvent ring behind
	  trace::emit / trace::visit_since).  It is the evidence base for CoreTest
	  event-sequence assertions and for cost attribution.

	  Turning it OFF makes trace::emit an inlined no-op: nothing is recorded and
	  the hot path pays zero cost.  Do that for performance measurement --
	  tracing perturbs exactly the paths a benchmark wants to measure.

config TRACE_CAPACITY
	int "Trace ring capacity (records)"
	default 1024
	range 64 8192
	help
	  Fixed capacity of the structured Core trace ring, in records.  The ring
	  storage lives in Core BSS whether or not CONFIG_TRACE is on, so this
	  still sizes the image when tracing is compiled out.

	  The value travels to the Core crate as one resolved number (not a Cargo
	  feature): genmk.py emits KCFG_TRACE_CAPACITY, the Makefile passes it to
	  os/core/build.rs, and build.rs validates it before writing the Rust
	  constant.  1024 records cover a full boot plus one core_test round.

config SELFTEST
	bool "Build the ArchTest selftest image"
	default n
	depends on VM_MMU
	help
	  Swap the boot entrypoint so the image runs the architectural selftests
	  (ArchTest) instead of entering the interactive Core Monitor.  Requires
	  the MMU profile: the selftests exercise page tables and do not build
	  against NoMMU.

endmenu
